<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lhokseumawe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lhokseumawe is a city on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> province in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. The remains of Samudera Pasai, one of the first Muslim states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, including the tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Malik al-Salih dated 1297, lie nearby. In the late 20th century it grew as the centre of a large natural gas industry based on the Arun field.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lhokseumawe.jpg" alt="Lhokseumawe" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Lhokseumawe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masjid_Islamic_Center_Lhokseumawe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
